    "publishedAt": "2026-11-10",
    "summary": "AMD announced the AMD EPYC Embedded 9006 Series SP7 CPUs, expanding its x86 processor portfolio optimized for embedded customer requirements and deployments. Advanced by the high-performance \"Zen 6\" core architecture, AMD EPYC Embedded 9006 CPUs combine up to 256 cores, scalable PCIe Gen 6 and CXL 3.1 connectivity, and advanced security from secure boot through runtime. With a throughput increase of up to 1.8x compared with the previous generation 5th Gen AMD EPYC 9005 Series processors, they provide the leadership compute and high-speed connectivity needed to scale throughput and handle increasingly demanding workloads in semiconductor automated test equipment (ATE), enterprise storage and network firewall applications. As AI infrastructure expands and data volumes grow, semiconductor ATE needs to validate memory and I/O devices faster, firewalls need to process and secure more network traffic, and storage controllers need to move and process more data.",
